{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK12DpopVerifierO","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DpopVerifier"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration","symbolKind":"enum","title":"DpopVerifier","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DpopVerifier","kind":"identifier"}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"DPoP proof verification — CONTRACT.md §21.7.2 (RFC 9449), contract 1.16."}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DpopVerifier","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The resource-server half of DPoP: given the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DPoP"},{"text":" header a caller presented, decide","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whether it proves possession for ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" request and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" access token, and return","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the key thumbprint that ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AxiamRequestAuthenticator\/verifyTokenBinding(_:proofs:)"},{"text":" then","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"matches against the token’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cnf.jkt"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Why this lives in the SDK","anchor":"Why-this-lives-in-the-SDK","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"§21.7.2 is a ten-check list, and the contract is blunt about partial implementations:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"“Partial verification is worse than none, because it produces a guard that reports","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"success.”","type":"text"}]},{"text":" Nine of the ten look optional until someone builds an attack out of the one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that was skipped, so they belong in one audited place rather than in every application","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"guarding an endpoint.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The two most often missing: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"typ"},{"type":"text","text":" — without pinning it to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dpop+jwt"},{"type":"text","text":", any "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"other","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" JWT"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"signed by the same key (an access token, an ID token) is replayable as a proof; and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ath"},{"type":"text","text":" — without it, a proof captured on one request can be re-aimed at a different token"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"held by the same key."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"The algorithm comes from the key, never from the header","anchor":"The-algorithm-comes-from-the-key-never-from-the-header","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"alg: none"},{"type":"text","text":" and RSA-public-key-as-HMAC-secret are the same bug wearing different clothes:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"the token told the verifier how to check the token","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":". This enum dispatches on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"embedded key’s own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kty"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"crv"},{"type":"text","text":", so an HMAC path is never reachable no matter what the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"header says."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/dpopverifier"]}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/Request"],"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/iatLeeway"],"anchor":"Type-Properties","title":"Type Properties","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/accessTokenHash(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/canonicalHtu(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/thumbprintS256(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/verifyProof(_:request:jtiStore:)"],"anchor":"Type-Methods","title":"Type Methods","generated":true}],"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk","title":"AxiamSDK","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/DpopVerifier/Request":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Request"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/dpopverifier\/request","title":"DpopVerifier.Request","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/verifyProof(_:request:jtiStore:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" needs to know about the current request."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamS